"Conan!" you whisper, "the rifle...shoot!"
By shaking hands Conan took father's double-barrelled rifle, pointed it at the beast... It occurred to you, that it might be tough to kill the predator. Maybe it's better to scare him off?
"Wait, don't shoot at him, shoot in the air!"
In another situation, Conan would probably argue, but now he is too scared. A shot rang out. The beast abruptly wheezed and stepped back.
"Shoot again, with another barrel! Get lost, dog, buzz off, A-A-A-A!"
Conan shoots once again. You can hear screams of animals, running away deeper in the forest. You shout as loud as possible, advancing towards the predator. And when you thought that you are done for, the beast wavered. Frightful burning eyes are vanished in the thicket, and thunderous silence fell upon the glade.   